Athletic Majors & Careers Join the Email List Meet the Coaches & Staff Contact Visit Request Information Apply Canvas Directory Maps Employment Give Alumni Career & Professional Development At Shenandoah University Home Students Employers Alumni Faculty Career & Professional Development equips students and alumni to build workforce-ready skills and pursue meaningful professional pathways through strategic coaching, professional programs, academic alignment, and intentional faculty and employer partnerships. Make An Appointment About SU Graduates SU Success Stories Welcome to Career & Professional Development! Major & Career Exploration Career Education Job & Internship Search Prepare For Graduate School Meet the Staff Upcoming Events Take the First Destinations Survey Experiential Learning Shenandoah University Career & Professional Development equips students and alumni to build workforce-ready skills and pursue meaningful professional pathways through strategic coaching, professional programs, academic alignment, and intentional faculty and employer partnerships. Career & Professional Development works with students and alumni in all aspects of the career development process, from choosing a major to career changes. Career development is a lifelong process influenced by all aspects of life, with the end result being high quality of life and personal satisfaction. Services offered include career exploration, experiential learning through internships, volunteer, summer and part-time opportunities, as well as resume building, interview skills workshops, graduate school search assistance, job search assistance, and professional headshots. Make an Appointment with Career & Professional Development Contact Us Monday-Friday, 9 a.m. – 5 p.m. 540-665-5412 | career@su.edu 314 Cooley Hall 1460 University Drive Winchester, VA 22601 Success Begins With SU Shenandoah prepares graduates for successful careers no matter which path their journey leads. View the 2025 Graduation Stats Learn more about the Class of 2025’s post-graduation plans and insights into students’ initial pathways beyond the school. This platform is Shenandoah University’s online job posting site where you can search for experiences (full-time, part-time, internships, volunteer, and more), register for Career & Professional Development events, and connect with employers who want to hire you! Visit Handshake for Students Are you an employer looking to hire a Shenandoah student? Create an account in Handshake. Visit Handshake for Employers Upcoming Events Academic Internships 101 with Inova (Friday, September 18th 2026, 12:00 pm – 1:00 pm EDT) When: Friday, September 18th 2026, 12:00 pm – 1:00 pm EDT Location: Virtual Are you in a non-clinical program (business, healthcare management, etc.) looking for an internship? Join Nate Mart, Inova's Program Manager for Academic Internships. Learn about where Inova internships are offered, how to submit […] Academic Internships 101 with Inova (Thursday, September 17th 2026, 12:00 pm – 1:00 pm EDT) When: Thursday, September 17th 2026, 12:00 pm – 1:00 pm EDT Location: Virtual Are you in a non-clinical program (business, healthcare management, etc.) looking for an internship? Join Nate Mart, Inova's Program Manager for Academic Internships. Learn about where Inova internships are offered, how to submit […] Career Lab (Thursday, September 17th 2026, 10:00 am – 11:00 am EDT) When: Thursday, September 17th 2026, 10:00 am – 11:00 am EDT Location: 702 University Drive, Winchester, Virginia 22601, United States Join Career & Professional Development for a Career Lab introducing the services and resources available to support your career journey. Learn how CPD can help […] Career Lab (Wednesday, September 16th 2026, 10:00 am – 11:00 am EDT) When: Wednesday, September 16th 2026, 10:00 am – 11:00 am EDT Location: University Drive, Winchester, Virginia 22601, United States Join Career & Professional Development for a Career Lab introducing the services and resources available to support your career journey. Learn how CPD can help with […] Follow Us Instagram Facebook X YouTube Quick Links Experience Shenandoah About Us Mission & Vision Strategic Plan 2030 Accreditation Online Privacy Policy & Practices Admissions Contact Admissions Visit Shenandoah Conservatory Audition Requirements Campus Map Admitted Students Get Social with SU Admissions Find Local Hotels Academics All Programs & Majors Search For Courses Health Care Programs Online Programs Athletic Majors & Careers Undecided Students Registering Courses as a Visiting Student Academic Calendars Academic Catalogs Faculty Directory Learning Support Services All-Steinway School Transformative Teaching & Learning Commencement Office of the President University Libraries Smith Library Hours Databases and e-Resources Research Guides Ask Us Hornet Central Tuition & Fees Payment Plan Transcript Request Parent/Person Proxy Office of the Registrar Online Services Technology Information Technology IT Policy iMLearning IT Help Desk Login to Hornet Hub Login to Canvas Login to WEPA Campus Life Events Calendar Athletics Calendar Performance Calendar Join a Club Intramural Sports Worship Services Campus Bookstore Student Services Career & Professional Development Disability Services Health & Safety Student of Concern Student Safety Tips Title IX & Sexual Misconduct Policy Dining & Catering Services University News Shenandoah Today What’s New at SU SU Quick Facts SU Google Extension Favorites Campus Bookstore SU Chrome Browser Extension Campus in Google Maps Find Local Hotels Employment Opportunities Events Calendar Apply for GCP Taking Care of Business Parking Permits Submit a Work Order Employee Departmental Forms Departments & Offices Room Reservations Conservatory Venue Reservations Filing a Complaint Emergency Information Campus Safety Emergency Operations Plan Sign Up for Emergency Alerts Campus Closure Policy Safety & Threat Notification Form Accessibility 1460